  abstract = {As part of a large, baseline assessment battery for a prospective study of offspring of alcoholics, the 27-item Young Adult Alcohol Problems Screening Test (YAAPST) was given to 490 college freshmen; approximately 9 mo later, 482 Ss completed the scale again. The YAAPST was designed to assess drinking consequences over 2 different time frames and also to indicate the frequency of occurrence during the past year. Results indicate that the YAAPST is a unidimensional scale with good psychometric properties (good internal consistency and test-retest reliability). Three different approaches were used to demonstrate the validity of the YAAPST. Findings support criterion validity, concurrent validity, and construct validity.},
